{"id":"G2030","lemma":"ἐπόπτης","transliteration":"epoptēs","sayIt":"epoptēs","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"eyewitness","meaning":"ἐπόπτης, -ου, ὁ\n[in LXX (of God): Est.5:1, 2Ma.3:39 2Mac 7:35, 3Ma.2:21 * ;]\n1. an overseer (LXX, ll. with).\n2. a spectator: 2Pe.1:16 (of ἐ. as applied to God, see parallels in Inscr., MM, Exp., xiv; of the use of this term in the mysteries, see Mayor on 2Pe, l.with; Thayer, see word).†\n(AS)","glosses":["eyewitnesses"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"2pe-1","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"eyewitnesses","kjv":"yewitnesses"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"2 Peter 1:16","note":"For we didn’t follow cunningly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of his majesty.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20300","lemma":"ἐκδικησία","transliteration":"ekdikēsia","gloss":"to avenge"},{"id":"G20301","lemma":"ἐκζητητής","transliteration":"ekzētētēs","gloss":"searcher out"},{"id":"G20303","lemma":"ἐκθλιβή","transliteration":"ekthlibē","gloss":"oppression"},{"id":"G20304","lemma":"ἔκθλιψις","transliteration":"ekthlipsis","gloss":"elision"},{"id":"G20305","lemma":"ἐκκοσμέω","transliteration":"ekkosmeō","gloss":"to adorn"},{"id":"G20306","lemma":"ἔκλαμπρος","transliteration":"eklampros","gloss":"very bright"},{"id":"G20307","lemma":"ἔκλαμψις","transliteration":"eklampsis","gloss":"sudden development"},{"id":"G20308","lemma":"ἐκλεκτόω","transliteration":"eklektoō","gloss":"to purify"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}